        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3fac87de-6398-5df8-8ebd-0c78511558a4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: H. G. Wells, Rubén Darío, Ángel de Estrada, Gabriele D'Annunzio\n- Works: Love and Mr Lewisham\n- Topics: modernismo\n\nFacts:\n- H. G. Wells, born Herbert George Wells on 21 September 1866 and died on 13 August 1946, was an English writer.\n- Rubén Darío, born Félix Rubén García Sarmiento on 18 January 1867 and died on 6 February 1916, was a Nicaraguan poet.\n- Rubén Darío initiated the Spanish-American literary movement called modernismo, which flourished at the end of the 19th century.\n- Love and Mr Lewisham, subtitled \"The Story of a Very Young Couple,\" is a 1900 novel by H. G. Wells set in the 1880s.\n- Ángel de Estrada was a great admirer and friend of Rubén Darío.\n- Ángel de Estrada was heavily influenced by the Italian writer Gabriele D'Annunzio.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
